            <div xml:id="d23">

                <pb facs="0111" n="26" xml:id="pg26"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">837.00/1548: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Minister in
                        Cuba</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Gonzales</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-05-13T18:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">May 13, 1919, 6
                                p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>Your May 11, midnight. You may inform General Crowder that Department strongly
                    advocates enactment of a law which will invalidate all nominations made in this
                    calendar year. The Department is inclined to recognize only nominations made in
                    the calendar year in which the election is held and then only when such
                    nominations have been made by conventions newly constituted in the entirety
                    within that year for that special purpose.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Polk</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
